Stage 5.2 (2026-08-03): atomic.ecsv replaced atomic.xml as the file ALIS
reads.

ECSV is plain text with a self-describing header, so the table can be read
and edited without a VOTable parser, and there is no hand-maintained "nrows"
attribute to fall out of step with the data.

atomic.ecsv is atomic.xml transcribed unchanged (815 rows), plus exactly 15
3He I lines taken from RJC's atomic_rjc2.xml -- the 3He isotope structure of
He I 6678 and 7065, and three EUV lines (515.6440, 522.2406, 537.0581).
830 rows in total. Every other value, including the O I 918-920 wavelengths
and the 10834.374575 3He line, is the default file's.

atomic.xml is kept for reference and is still accepted by "run atomic", but
reading it prints a deprecation warning. To bring your own file forward:

    python convert_xmlFormat_to_ecsvFormat.py yours.xml yours.ecsv

The converter checks its own output cell by cell against the source and
fails if anything differs, and reports any transition listed under more than
one MassNumber. The shipped file has four such groups (6/7Li, 12/13C,
54/56/57/58Fe) which are genuine isotopes, not duplicates.

